# Ozark Plant Hub — secrets & settings.
# Copy this file to "hub.env" (same folder) and fill in what you use, then restart the hub.
# Keep hub.env PRIVATE — it holds your secrets. (OS environment variables, if set, win over this file.)

# --- Hub access key: REQUIRED. Only devices that send this same key can read/write data. ---
# The hub is fail-CLOSED: if this is blank/missing, sync + SMS + email + payments REFUSE every request
# (a typo here must never silently publish the customer database). Pick a long random string.
OZARK_HUB_KEY=

# --- Card processor: fill in ONE set ---
# Square (self-serve):
OZARK_SQUARE_TOKEN=
OZARK_SQUARE_LOCATION=
OZARK_SQUARE_ENV=sandbox
# Helcim (value pick, also self-serve):
# OZARK_HELCIM_TOKEN=
# CardPointe / Fiserv (fallback):
# OZARK_CARDPOINTE_SITE=
# OZARK_CARDPOINTE_MID=
# OZARK_CARDPOINTE_USER=
# OZARK_CARDPOINTE_PASS=
# OZARK_CARDPOINTE_ENV=uat

# --- 💳🏦 CardPointe FUNDING (read-only deposit reconcile — see CARDPOINTE-FUNDING-SETUP.md) ---
# Reuses the CardPointe creds above by default (CardConnect issues them customer-level: one set covers
# every MID under your customer id). Usually you only need the MIDs + env=prod; leave the rest unless
# CardConnect gives you a separate funding credential or host.
# OZARK_CPFUND_ENV=prod                 # prod = fts.cardconnect.com · uat = fts-uat.cardconnect.com
# OZARK_CPFUND_MID_1=       # Arkadelphia funding MID
# OZARK_CPFUND_MID_2=       # Hot Springs funding MID
# OZARK_CPFUND_USER=                    # only if funding uses a DIFFERENT credential than processing
# OZARK_CPFUND_PASS=
# OZARK_CPFUND_HOST=                    # only to override the fts host (tests point this at 127.0.0.1)

# --- Texting (Twilio) ---
OZARK_TWILIO_SID=
OZARK_TWILIO_TOKEN=
OZARK_TWILIO_FROM=

# --- Email / SMTP (for A/R statements) ---
# Company address on SiteGround (recommended): use the MAILBOX's normal password.
#   OZARK_SMTP_USER=owner@example.com
# Gmail instead: use a Google APP PASSWORD (16 chars, needs 2-Step Verification on) — not the normal one.
# The mail server is auto-picked from the address (gmail -> smtp.gmail.com, else mail.<domain>); override
# with OZARK_SMTP_HOST/PORT only if a test fails. This only lets the hub SEND — it never touches DNS/MX.
OZARK_SMTP_USER=
OZARK_SMTP_PASS=
OZARK_SMTP_FROM=Ozark Cleaners and Laundry
# OZARK_SMTP_HOST=mail.cleaners.example.com
# OZARK_SMTP_PORT=465
# Cloud hubs (DigitalOcean) BLOCK direct email ports — set these two and the hub sends through the tiny
# HTTPS relay page on SiteGround instead (siteground-mail-relay.php; see EMAIL-SETUP.md). Same key in both.
# OZARK_MAIL_RELAY_URL=https://relay.cleaners.example.com/index.php
# OZARK_MAIL_RELAY_KEY=

# --- Optional ---
# OZARK_PORT=8090

# 📬 Migration forwarder (2026-08-31): a signed copy of every verified inbound SMS is relayed to this URL
# (the OLD system, SMRT) so both inboxes see everything during the migration. Unset = no forwarding — the
# end-state once SMRT is retired.
OZARK_SMS_FORWARD_URL=

# --- 📗 QuickBooks Online (read-only accounting — see QUICKBOOKS-SETUP.md) ---
# From the Intuit Developer app the OWNER creates (developer.intuit.com). Read-only: the hub only PULLS the
# Profit & Loss to feed the open-books page and reconcile against the register. Secrets stay HERE, never in
# the repo/app. Restart the hub after setting these, then connect once from /api/qb/connect.
# OZARK_QBO_CLIENT_ID=
# OZARK_QBO_CLIENT_SECRET=
# OZARK_QBO_ENV=production
# The EXACT https callback registered in the Intuit app (must match character-for-character):
# OZARK_QBO_REDIRECT=https://hub.example.com/api/qb/callback

# 📦 the 24/7 drop box (DROP-BOX-DESIGN.md) — the BOX's own credential, never the hub key.
# Unset = every /api/dropbox box endpoint refuses. Any long random string; rotate per box if one is ever stolen.
# OZARK_DROPBOX_KEY=
